<%# The button = possibility × permission: the machine's transitions_from
    crossed with the role's can?. Guards do not gate the render — a
    metadata-reading guard refuses input, not possibility, and the refusal
    is the flash's job. Rendered INSIDE the card's metadata form — each
    button aims its own action via formaction, so the submitted fields ride
    with whichever is clicked. Locals: record, fire_url (event_name -> url). %>
<div class="transition-buttons">
  <% permitted_actions(record).each do |event_name| %>
    <button type="submit" class="transition-button"
            formaction="<%= fire_url.call(event_name) %>" formmethod="post">
      <%= event_name %>
    </button>
  <% end %>
</div>
